('horse','HRS','Horse','swift','default','common','born to gallop',
 '{"facts":["Horses were first domesticated on the Eurasian steppe roughly 5,500 years ago","A horse can doze standing up thanks to a locking system of tendons and ligaments called the stay apparatus","Racing Quarter Horses have been clocked at over 70 km/h in short sprints"],"habitat":"open grasslands, now almost every landscape alongside people","size":"1.4–1.8 m at the withers, 400–600 kg","superpower":"a stride built for the long open road","india_note":"the Marwari of Rajasthan, with its inward-curving ears, and the Kathiawari of Gujarat are India''s own breeds"}',
 false, 11),
('blackbuck','BBK','Blackbuck','swift','default','uncommon','the spiral-horned sprinter',
